# Oman conditional validation

## Source of truth

- Analysis sheet **Conditional Validations** + [PINT OM](https://test-docs.peppol.eu/pint/pint-om/2026-Q2-v1.0.1/pint-om/)
- Skill: `add-conditional-validation-case` + `expand-omn-conditional-rule` (+ inventory `reference.md`)

## Allowed

- Rule IDs ending in `-OM` / `ALIGNED-IBRP-*-OM` / `IBR-*-OM` (and CL if truly if-then)
- Every scenario **must** include `ruleId`
- Titles: `Excel upload · Covoro | {ruleId} | {condition} → {accepted|error file}`
- Covoro template **header** keys (row 4), Oman dropdown labels from `Master.omnCore.ts`

## Forbidden (UAE)

- Emirates ID, Cabinet Decision, BTUAE-*, UAE TIN 0235, UAE emirate subdivisions
- FTZ / Beneficiary UAE matrices, AE-only IBR / IBR-*-AE
- Inventing UAE fillers when an Oman rule is formula/backend-only

## Triage before coding

| Kind | Destination |
|------|-------------|
| If A → B required/forbidden | This suite |
| Σ / taxable amount / tax amount math | Formula suite |
| Code list only (`CL-*`) | Field validation |
| Category Backend / no Excel field | Skip + note in skill reference |

## Agent scope

- One rule group (or one `ruleId`) per turn unless the user approved a batch
- Config in `ConditionalValidation.ts` → builder in `conditionalValidationHelper.ts` → thin describe in spec
